{start_of_verse label="Verse 1"}
[G]Dashing through the snow
In a one-horse open [C]sleigh,
O'er the hills we [D]go,
Laughing all the [G]way;
Bells on bob tail ring,
Making spirits [C]bright,
Oh what sport to [D]ride and sing
A sleighing song to[G]night!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]Jingle bells, jingle bells,
Jingle all the way!
[C]Oh, what joy it is to [G]ride
In a [D]one-horse open sleigh!
[G]Jingle bells, jingle bells,
Jingle all the way!
[C]Oh, what joy it is to [G]ride
In a [D]one-horse open [G]sleigh!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 2"}
[G]A day or two ago
I thought I'd take a [C]ride,
And soon Miss Fanny [D]Bright
Was seated by my [G]side;
The horse was lean and lank,
Misfortune seemed his [C]lot,
He got into a [D]drifted bank,
And we, we got up[G]sot.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 3"}
[G]Now the ground is white,
Go it while you're [C]young,
Take the girls to[D]night,
And sing this sleighing [G]song;
Just get a bob-tailed bay,
Two-forty as his [C]speed,
Hitch him to an [D]open sleigh
And snap! you'll take the [G]lead.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
{x_end: G}
